oid  now let's look at a few figures and  understand if their prisms are not  remember the definition identical  parallel ends and all flat surfaces  here's the first figure it's a part of a  pipe both the ends are circles and up  parallel to each other it means that  this figure has identical parallel ends  this figure has identical parallel ends  but has a curved surface hence it's not  a prism I want to emphasize there are  only two things that make a  three-dimensional shape a prism  identical and parallel ends and all its  phases flat here the ends are flat but  the surface is curved so it's not a  prism here's another figure first we  look at the ends  both are triangles and hence we can say  that this figure has identical ends but  wait they are not parallel the upper  triangle is slightly tilted so this  figure as well is not a prism now assume  we have a plane with a rectangle on it  if we project the rectangle upwards  equally from all sides we get a prism in  this figure we have projected all the  sides to the same height but what if we  do not project all the sides to equal  Heights if we do not project it equally  like in this figure we do not get a  prism this is not a prism as its ends  are not parallel
 

